🟠 pg in data (prod-eu-1) keeps crashing because volume claim pg-data is out of space. It fails with "PANIC: could not write to file "pg_wal/xlogtemp.31": No space left on device". Its last run lasted ten seconds; two restarts since its pod was created one hour ago. Fix: raise the storage request of persistentvolumeclaim/pg-data above 10Gi. To check the size and capacity of the full volume claim, run kubectl describe pvc pg-data -n data
🟠 pg in data (prod-eu-1) keeps crashing because volume claim pg-data is out of space.
| 🟠 pg in **data** (**prod-eu-1**) keeps crashing because volume claim **pg-data** is out of space.
| It fails with `PANIC: could not write to file "pg_wal/xlogtemp.31": No space left on device`.
| Its last run lasted ten seconds; two restarts since its pod was created one hour ago.
| Fix: raise the storage request of persistentvolumeclaim/pg-data above 10Gi.
| To check the size and capacity of the full volume claim, run
| ```
| kubectl describe pvc pg-data -n data
| ```
